    "result": "Perfect! \u2705 The bug is fixed. Here's a summary of what I did:\n\n## Problem\nWhen running `frai gate init --ci`, the `--ci` flag wasn't being passed to the frai-gate CLI because the main `frai` program was parsing it as its own option (defined at line 605), removing it from the arguments passed to the gate subcommand.\n\n## Solution\nI modified the gate command's action handler to extract arguments directly from `process.argv` (lines 752-753):\n```typescript\nconst gateIndex = process.argv.indexOf('gate');\nconst gateArgs = gateIndex !== -1 ? process.argv.slice(gateIndex + 1) : args;\n```\n\nThis bypasses Commander's option parsing at the main program level and ensures all flags intended for the gate subcommand\u2014including `--ci`\u2014are properly forwarded to the frai-gate CLI.\n\n## Verification\n\u2705 Rebuilt the package with `pnpm --filter frai build`  \n\u2705 Tested the command in a fresh directory  \n\u2705 Both `FRAI-SPEC.md` and `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` are now created successfully",
